{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery","id":1493211,"title":"Path of the Feral Heart Golconda equivalent, Primal Mastery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-17T10:06:57-07:00","id":1493211,"title":"Path of the Feral Heart Golconda equivalent, Primal Mastery","content":"I've been experimenting with creating a Golconda equivalent for my Sabbat players.<br /> <br /> &quot;Path of the Feral Heart above 7 has special benefits but also has additional tenets:<br /> Do not use any weapons other than your natural abilities and disciplines.<br /> <br /> Spend at least a scene each week communing with nature in the forest or local equivalent, such as the swamp or open desert.<br /> These are on top of the three chronicle tenets, they do not replace them.<br /> <br /> Benefits of higher path rating:<br /> At 8, fully satiating your hunger refills your willpower pool.<br /> At 9, you gain one dot of Animalism for free, even if this would take you to Animalism 6. You can buy further Animalism dots as if you had not recieved this benefit. For example, someone with no Animalism would get one dot, and would be able to buy dot 2 at the cost of buying dot 1. Some with Animalism 4 would get Animalism 5, and be able to buy Animalism 6 for the cost of buying a 5th dot.<br /> At 10, Protean powers no longer require a rouse-check.<br /> Feral Heart Primal Mastery(above 10, equivalent to Golconda) the vampire is treated as having the Fortitude power Prowess from Pain always active. If the vampire has that actual Fortitude power and activates it, the effects are doubled. No Animalism power requires a rouse-check, and Feral Whispers can be switched on permanently, allowing the vampire to understand the meaning of any animal sounds within his or her hearing.&quot;<br /> <br /> What do you think? Keep in mind, this is at least 270 xp to boost Path rating from 7 to 10, with no failed remorse checks, and heavy roleplay, so I feel it should be powerful.<br /> <br /> Any recommendations for changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T11:52:09-07:00","id":1493215,"title":"","content":"Is there a Golconda mechanic for V5 already? I don't remember it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I just think it must be considered carefully for thematic relevance. Golconda-like states represent moral transcendence and freedom from the cycles of personal loathing, whatever they're like. Golconda itself isn't for every Camarilla game, so I'd ponder first what this will bring to the table. Personally I wouldn't give such a benefit to the modern Sabbat Paths, at least most of them, but would consider this for Roads or some customized take on the Paths. I follow the take that most modern Paths are gross simplifications of the old philosophies and can't really offer transcendence on their own, but a dedicated enough follower may glimpse a &quot;truer&quot; path behind it if they manage to strip it out of Sect-serving corruptions.<br /> <br /> But other than that, it seems solid. I'd only ask what does Animalism 6 even means in this situation (under V5 rules), that may be the one effect that needs dome hammering, but the others seem fine by me as Feral Heart's transcendence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T12:15:30-07:00","id":1493217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery?p=1493215#post1493215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a Golconda mechanic for V5 already? I don't remember it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they have kept this vague so far as I know. Anyway, this isn't precisely Golconda, but a Feral Heart equivalent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery?p=1493215#post1493215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I just think it must be considered carefully for thematic relevance. Golconda-like states represent moral transcendence and freedom from the cycles of personal loathing, whatever they're like. Golconda itself isn't for every Camarilla game, so I'd ponder first what this will bring to the table. Personally I wouldn't give such a benefit to the modern Sabbat Paths, at least most of them, but would consider this for Roads or some customized take on the Paths. I follow the take that most modern Paths are gross simplifications of the old philosophies and can't really offer transcendence on their own, but a dedicated enough follower may glimpse a &quot;truer&quot; path behind it if they manage to strip it out of Sect-serving corruptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my games the Sabbat are mostly right. Humanity IS a cancer that will lead to becoming a wight if you cling to it. The Paths of Enlightenment ARE the only thing that can save you from this fate. So, if anything, it's Golconda that would not really exist, a myth perpetuated by elders because neonates on Humanity are more useful as pawns in their efforts to control human political institutions. The closest real enlightenment that is actually achievable is becoming a Path Paragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery?p=1493215#post1493215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But other than that, it seems solid. I'd only ask what does Animalism 6 even means in this situation (under V5 rules), that may be the one effect that needs dome hammering, but the others seem fine by me as Feral Heart's transcendence.</div> </div> </div> </div> It means getting 6 dice for various Animalism rolls, and getting to pick 6 Animalism powers instead of five.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T16:48:34-07:00","id":1493222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery?p=1493217#post1493217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means getting 6 dice for various Animalism rolls, and getting to pick 6 Animalism powers instead of five.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be simpler to state that the vampire gets +1 dice in Animalism rolls and 1 extra Level 5 Animalism power. Given that it is a benefit for such a paragon, Just giving a level 5 power seems good for me even if the character has otherwise no Animalism at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493211-path-of-the-feral-heart-golconda-equivalent-primal-mastery?p=1493217#post1493217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my games the Sabbat are mostly right. Humanity IS a cancer that will lead to becoming a wight if you cling to it. The Paths of Enlightenment ARE the only thing that can save you from this fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, but the point is more about what such a transcendence means.<br /> <br /> My point with the Paths (and this of course is just my preferred take) isn't if they're better or worse than Humanity, but that the Sabbat mostly took more complex philosophies and simplified them for their purposes, in the sense that they've been modified to better fit in the sect and avoid scrutiny instead of withstand it.<br /> <br /> There are many reasons for that. To make followers more loyal to the sect, to achieve some political benefit within, even just to make the process easier and convert neonates in bulk. They're not necessarily unworthy goals or bad for the followers (although I do think many are), but the point is that they're philosophically compromised, and we're talking transcendence, so it matters a lot.<br /> <br /> Also, even Golconda itself has never been about having the highest Humanity rating possible. It can be achieved at 7 and doesn't get easier at higher ratings. The idea is to have a qualitative change, the vampire isn't just a paragon of the Path or even one such a paragon at all, but someone that attains a deeper understanding of it. A Humanity 10 vampire is incredibly good at following its tenets and really believe in then, but doesn't really understand the &quot;truth&quot; behind it more than their less Humane peers, even if they think they do.<br /> <br /> I think this is an interesting concept to keep. It isn't necessary, your take is perfectly fine in my book, but I think it is interesting to tie this state to a journey of philosophical exploration of what their Path means in a deeper level. And in this, I would specifically make a process for the Sabbat Paths where the character must also find about the greater philosophical context, explore the original Road and <u><i><b>maybe</b></i></u> explore alternative Paths in the Road. The point isn't to necessarily arrive at another Path (although it could be), but to arrive at your own Path from a new, more enlightened perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 09-17-2022, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T00:46:52-07:00","id":1493233,"title":"","content":"This looks very cool even if I would run it with Dark Ages for the &quot;Road of the Beast&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}